 "notes": [
  "The 'uno:2 floats when the button is open' warning is not a real problem for this manual, so I kept the graph unchanged and added no resistor. The tutorial is about INPUT_PULLUP: pinMode(2, INPUT_PULLUP) turns on the ATmega's internal pull-up to 5V on pin 2, which holds the pin HIGH when the button is open. The tutorial text says this, and its hardware list has only the board, a button, a breadboard and hook-up wire. An external resistor would break the 'exactly the parts the tutorial says' rule.",
  "Parts are the same as in step 1; none added or dropped.",
  "The button straddles the centre gap. Side 1 (1.l, 1.r) is in the top half at columns 10 and 11. Side 2 (2.l, 2.r) is in the bottom half at the same columns.",
  "Pin 2 goes by wire2 to the button's top side (10t.a). GND goes by wire1 to the button's bottom side (10b.j). Pressing the button joins pin 2 to GND, as the text describes.",
  "The exact breadboard columns and rows are my choice. The image only shows the wires reaching the button area.",
  "The LED is the onboard pin-13 LED, so it has no edges. The text only says 'ground', so the choice of GND.1 on the Uno is an assumption."
 ],
